  "title": "iEEG during direct electrical stimulation of orbitofrontal and other sites (Rao, Sellers et al., 2018): continuous-stimulation and single-pulse recordings",
  "description": "Intracranial EEG (ECoG grids/strips and depth electrodes) recorded from 17 adults undergoing inpatient seizure-localization monitoring. Recordings were made before, during and after continuous 100 Hz direct electrical stimulation of the lateral orbitofrontal cortex and other sites, as well as during single-pulse electrical stimulation. The dataset supports study of how orbitofrontal stimulation acutely affects mood in individuals with depressive symptoms.",
  "methods_description": "Data were recorded with Natus clinical, Tucker-Davis Technologies, and NeuroOmega systems. Stimulation amplitude and site are encoded per run. Original float64 MATLAB v7.3 files were converted to BrainVision float32 with no filtering, resampling, or re-referencing. Channel and electrode tables come from the release.",
